e county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that pair came in at 58% of normal, and November to December at 46%. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 72% of normal on the middle of the grids. On grid 22705 the driest year was 1965, at 71% of normal.</p>"}
